1. e4 e5 2. Nf3 Nc6 3. Bc4 Nf6 4. Ng5 d5 5. exd5 Nd4
( 5... b5 6. Bf1 { Retreats out of the pawn's reach. The pawn on b5 is now loose, because the bishop on f1 looks straight at it. } 6... Nxd5 7. Bxb5 { Wins the loose pawn and attacks the knight on c6, which is the piece guarding e5. } 7... Bb7 8. d4 exd4 9. O-O )
6. c3 { Kicks the knight off d4, where it was eyeing the bishop and the c2 square. } 6... b5 7. Bf1 { Steps out of the way of the b-pawn and keeps an eye on the pawn on b5. } 7... Nxd5 8. Ne4 { Saves the knight on g5, which the black queen now attacks. The pawn on c3 still hits the knight on d4. Plan: develop, castle and keep the extra pawn. } *
